# Transitive reachability — no warning when chain is consumed.
# Binding 'a' is defined in the first intermediate body.
# Binding 'b' references 'a' in the second intermediate body.
# The final expression references 'b', so both 'b' and 'a' are transitively
# reachable — no lost-binding warning should fire.
[call [fn [let x] [a: [+ x 1]] [b: [+ a 2]] b] 10]
=== out
Int(13)
